      "message": "In the design doc for NSD APIs for thread there\u0027s this:\n\n```\nIf {@link #FLAG_NO_AUTO_RENAME} is used in {@code flags}, {@link #FAILURE_SERVICE_NAME_CONFLICT}\nwill be reported if the service name has already been registered by another device or app with\ndifferent UID on the same device; and {@link FAILURE_HOST_NAME_CONFLICT} will be reported only when\nthe same host name has been registered by another device (there won\u0027t be an error if it\u0027s registered\nby another app on the same device)\n```\n\nI don\u0027t remember why the last thing was written though; if one app can register the same hostname, adding addresses to it, then it could interfere with the service registration of the first app, sending its clients to a different server ?\n\nThat doesn\u0027t seem right; this should probably fail the registration if there\u0027s a conflict due to service hostname when the UID of the registration is different ?\n\nThat should be easy to achieve by putting the uid in the Registration, and passing it from NsdService",
